export const MENU = "# Kitchy's menu (prices in EGP)\n\n## Mama Fatma (ماما فاطمة) - Egyptian classics, Shubra, Cairo. Cooking for her family of seven for 30 years. Her molokhia is famous on the whole street.\n- Koshari / كشري / Koshari [main] EGP 85, 25 min, serves 1, vegetarian. Egypt's favourite comfort food: layers of rice, brown lentils, macaroni and chickpeas, topped with a garlicky vinegar tomato sauce and a mountain of crispy fried onions. Hot sauce comes on the side. Ingredients: Rice, brown lentils, macaroni (wheat), chickpeas, tomatoes, garlic, vinegar, onions, sunflower oil, cumin, chilli. Allergens: gluten.\n- Molokhia with Chicken / ملوخية بالفراخ / Mouloukhiya au poulet [main] EGP 180, 40 min, serves 2. Finely minced jute leaves simmered in homemade chicken broth and finished with the famous \"tasha\" of garlic and coriander fried in ghee. Served with half a golden roast chicken and white vermicelli rice. Ingredients: Jute leaves, chicken, chicken broth, garlic, coriander, ghee (butter), rice, vermicelli (wheat), cardamom, bay leaf. Allergens: gluten, dairy.\n- Mixed Mahshi / محشي مشكل / Mahshi mixte [main] EGP 220, 45 min, serves 3, vegetarian. A family-size tray of vegetables hand-stuffed with herby rice seasoned with tomato, dill, parsley and mint, then slow-cooked in a light tomato broth. Every piece is rolled by hand. Ingredients: Rice, bell peppers, zucchini, eggplant, vine leaves, tomatoes, onions, dill, parsley, mint, olive oil, lemon. Allergens: none of the common allergens.\n- Beef Fatta / فتة باللحمة / Fatta au bœuf [main] EGP 240, 50 min, serves 2. The celebration dish of Eid: layers of toasted baladi bread soaked in beef broth, fluffy rice, and slow-cooked beef chunks, all covered with a tangy garlic-vinegar tomato sauce. Ingredients: Beef, baladi bread (wheat), rice, beef broth, garlic, vinegar, tomatoes, ghee (butter). Allergens: gluten, dairy.\n- Stuffed Pigeons / حمام محشي / Pigeons farcis [main] EGP 320, 60 min, serves 1. A proper Egyptian feast: two young pigeons stuffed with freekeh (green wheat) cooked in rich broth with onion and warm spices, simmered, then roasted until the skin is crisp and golden. Served with a bowl of the broth. Ingredients: Pigeons, freekeh (wheat), onions, ghee (butter), pigeon broth, cinnamon, cardamom, black pepper, mastic. Allergens: gluten, dairy.\n\n## Teta Samira (تيتا سميرة) - Alexandrian seafood, Anfoushi, Alexandria. A fisherman's daughter who buys the catch fresh every morning from the Anfoushi harbour.\n- Sayadeya Fish / صيادية سمك / Poisson sayadeya [seafood] EGP 260, 40 min, serves 1. The Alexandrian classic: fresh white fish fillets baked with cumin and lemon, served on rice cooked in a deep brown caramelised-onion fish stock. Topped with toasted pine nuts. Ingredients: White fish, rice, onions, fish stock, cumin, lemon, garlic, pine nuts, olive oil. Allergens: fish, nuts.\n- Crispy Fried Shrimp / جمبري مقلي مقرمش / Crevettes frites croustillantes [seafood] EGP 320, 25 min, serves 1. Large Mediterranean shrimp, marinated in garlic and lemon, coated in crunchy breadcrumbs and fried until golden. Served with homemade tahini sauce and a lemon wedge. Ingredients: Shrimp, breadcrumbs (wheat), eggs, garlic, lemon, sunflower oil, tahini (sesame), cumin. Allergens: shellfish, gluten, eggs, sesame.\n- Yellow Lentil Soup / شوربة عدس أصفر / Soupe de lentilles jaunes [healthy] EGP 60, 15 min, serves 1, vegetarian. Winter in a bowl: yellow lentils slowly cooked with carrot, onion and tomato, blended silky smooth and seasoned with cumin. Comes with lemon and a bag of crispy toasted bread. Ingredients: Yellow lentils, carrots, onions, tomatoes, cumin, vegetable broth, lemon, toasted bread (wheat). Allergens: gluten.\n- Seafood Rice Tagine / طاجن رز بالسي فود / Tajine de riz aux fruits de mer [seafood] EGP 350, 45 min, serves 2, spicy. A clay-pot tagine of shrimp, calamari rings and fish pieces baked with red rice, tomato, peppers and Alexandrian spices until the top turns crispy. Mildly spicy. Ingredients: Shrimp, calamari, white fish, rice, tomatoes, bell peppers, onions, garlic, chilli, cumin, olive oil. Allergens: shellfish, fish.\n\n## Om Karim (Mona) (أم كريم (منى)) - Oven-baked favourites, Nasr City, Cairo. Her wood-style oven turns out the crispiest roz moammar and the creamiest béchamel in Nasr City.\n- Roz Moammar with Chicken / رز معمر بالفراخ / Riz moammar au poulet [baked] EGP 200, 55 min, serves 2. Rice slow-baked in a clay pot with milk, cream and butter until the inside is silky and the top turns into a golden crust. Served with a quarter roast chicken. Ingredients: Rice, milk, cream, butter, chicken, onion, salt, black pepper. Allergens: dairy.\n- Hawawshi / حواوشي / Hawawshi [baked] EGP 120, 25 min, serves 1, spicy. Baladi bread stuffed with minced beef mixed with onions, peppers, parsley and a secret spice blend, then baked until the bread is crackling crisp. Served with pickles and tahini. Ingredients: Minced beef, baladi bread (wheat), onions, bell peppers, parsley, chilli, spices, tahini (sesame). Allergens: gluten, sesame.\n- Macaroni Béchamel / مكرونة بشاميل / Macaronis béchamel [baked] EGP 190, 40 min, serves 3. Penne layered with tomato-simmered minced beef and a thick, creamy béchamel, baked until the top is golden brown. The Sunday lunch every Egyptian grew up with. Ingredients: Penne pasta (wheat), minced beef, tomatoes, onions, milk, butter, wheat flour, eggs, nutmeg. Allergens: gluten, dairy, eggs.\n- Egyptian Moussaka / مسقعة / Moussaka égyptienne [main] EGP 110, 30 min, serves 2, vegetarian, spicy. Slices of fried eggplant and green peppers baked in a rich tomato, garlic and vinegar sauce. Fully plant-based and even better the next day. Served with baladi bread. Ingredients: Eggplant, green peppers, tomatoes, garlic, vinegar, chilli, sunflower oil, baladi bread (wheat). Allergens: gluten.\n\n## Nana Hoda (نانا هدى) - After-dinner desserts, Heliopolis, Cairo. Grandmother of eleven and the reason every family gathering ends with something sweet.\n- Om Ali / أم علي / Om Ali [desserts] EGP 90, 25 min, serves 1, vegetarian. Egypt's most loved dessert: crispy puff pastry soaked in sweet hot milk and cream, loaded with raisins, coconut, almonds, hazelnuts and pistachios, then baked until bubbling. Ingredients: Puff pastry (wheat, butter), milk, cream, sugar, raisins, coconut, almonds, hazelnuts, pistachios. Allergens: gluten, dairy, nuts.\n- Basbousa / بسبوسة / Basboussa [desserts] EGP 120, 10 min, serves 4, vegetarian. Soft, golden semolina cake made with yoghurt and coconut, soaked in rose-scented sugar syrup and topped with a whole almond on every piece. Box of 8 pieces. Ingredients: Semolina (wheat), yoghurt (milk), butter, coconut, sugar, rose water, almonds. Allergens: gluten, dairy, nuts.\n- Roz bel Laban / رز بلبن / Riz au lait [desserts] EGP 55, 10 min, serves 1, vegetarian. Short-grain rice slowly cooked in full-cream milk with a hint of vanilla and mastic, chilled and dusted with cinnamon. Available plain or baked with a caramelised top. Ingredients: Rice, full-cream milk, sugar, vanilla, mastic, cinnamon, cornstarch. Allergens: dairy.\n- Cream Konafa / كنافة بالقشطة / Konafa à la crème [desserts] EGP 140, 30 min, serves 3, vegetarian. Golden, buttery shredded kataifi pastry baked around a thick layer of fresh cream (ashta), drenched in cold syrup and sprinkled with crushed pistachios. Ingredients: Kataifi pastry (wheat), ghee (butter), fresh cream (milk), sugar, lemon, pistachios. Allergens: gluten, dairy, nuts.\n\n## Mama Nour (ماما نور) - Healthy & grilled, Maadi, Cairo. A nutritionist and mother of three who makes light, fresh food that still tastes like home.\n- Chicken Shawarma Plate / طبق شاورما فراخ / Assiette shawarma poulet [main] EGP 190, 30 min, serves 1. Chicken thighs marinated overnight in yoghurt, lemon and shawarma spices, seared and sliced thin. Served with homemade garlic toum, pickles, a fresh salad and warm bread. Ingredients: Chicken, yoghurt (milk), lemon, garlic, sunflower oil, shawarma spices, pickles, tomatoes, lettuce, bread (wheat). Allergens: gluten, dairy.\n- Green Garden Salad / سلطة خضرا / Salade du jardin [healthy] EGP 75, 10 min, serves 1, vegetarian. Crisp lettuce, cucumber, tomato, radish, rocket and fresh mint tossed in a lemon and extra-virgin olive oil dressing. Light, fresh, and free from common allergens. Ingredients: Lettuce, cucumber, tomatoes, radish, rocket, mint, lemon, extra-virgin olive oil, salt. Allergens: none of the common allergens.\n- Grilled Chicken & Veggies / فراخ مشوية بالخضار / Poulet grillé et légumes [healthy] EGP 210, 35 min, serves 1. Chicken thighs marinated overnight in lemon, garlic, thyme and a little yoghurt, grilled over charcoal, served with roasted zucchini, carrots and peppers. Ingredients: Chicken, yoghurt (milk), lemon, garlic, thyme, olive oil, zucchini, carrots, bell peppers. Allergens: dairy.\n- Charcoal Kofta / كفتة على الفحم / Kofta au charbon [main] EGP 230, 30 min, serves 1. Hand-shaped skewers of minced beef and lamb with onion, parsley and seven spices, grilled over charcoal. Served with tahini, pickles, baladi salad and bread. Ingredients: Minced beef, minced lamb, onions, parsley, seven spices, tahini (sesame), baladi bread (wheat), tomatoes, cucumber. Allergens: gluten, sesame.\n\n# Delivery\n- Delivery costs EGP 30. A customer's first 3 orders have free delivery.\n\n# Points and ranks\n- Customers earn 1 point per EGP 10 spent (after discounts, before delivery), times their rank multiplier.\n- Ranks by number of orders: starter 0+ orders x1; bronze 3+ orders x1.1; silver 10+ orders x1.25; gold 25+ orders x1.5; platinum 50+ orders x1.75; diamond 100+ orders x2.\n- Rewards (redeem in the Points tab, then pick the voucher in the cart): free_delivery: free delivery for 80 points; off_25: EGP 25 off for 100 points; pct_10: 10% off up to EGP 60 for 150 points (needs bronze rank); off_50: EGP 50 off for 180 points (needs bronze rank); pct_20: 20% off up to EGP 120 for 300 points (needs silver rank); off_100: EGP 100 off for 350 points (needs silver rank); pct_30: 30% off up to EGP 200 for 600 points (needs gold rank).";
